summary:
I read research/sf/population-system.md whole (1,091 lines) and checked about 600 claims against the host at 81f1cd96, the cited design documents and the map-side notes. The host HEAD was read from .git files; no git command was run. 18 claims do not hold: 3 WRONG, 1 UNSUPPORTED, 14 IMPRECISE, each with its evidence and an exact fix.

- **WRONG (3):** P-17's belief axes are FP's own lighting (FP_LIT_BELIEF), not pre-FP. In §12 V12, rules:1024 lies outside the range 1025-1030. In row P-13, two of the eight conquest flags are set in some presets, so 'none set' is false; the conjunction still holds in no preset, so the D cells stand.
- **UNSUPPORTED (1):** the quotation 'a per-settlement limit by tier' appears in no record.
- **IMPRECISE, notable:** SRD is premium-gated after all: canManageCampaigns means premium or elevated, the same gate LWG uses. The canon-at-birth open question and the proposal §6 citation are stale, since §6 was superseded and J386/J387 have ruled. The history-row text differs across the three dispersal producers. Pulse records also carry consequenceOutcomes. Steading growth to 401 takes up to 78 weeks, not 70. The deadband rate oscillates between about 0.0025 and 0.0035.
- **IMPRECISE, the rest:** several citation lines, two quotations and one stale line count.

Everything else holds:
- the M4 model and all its constants;
- the three dispatch callers and the approval path that never dispatches;
- the timelapse reading the deltas as a map when they are arrays;
- the overlay and the orbit dots;
- every preset cell in the §7 table;
- the calamity exposure law, the steading and first-class lanes, the war and razing constants and the conveyance;
- the Wave P constants (spot-checked);
- all 72 stated host line counts.

The record is at /home/user/maps-architecture/docs/validation/retrovalidation-2026-10-18/population-verify.md, and the LANDED line is appended to docs/lane-events.log.
